WEBVTT

00:00:01.910 --> 00:00:03.550
I can't take it anymore!

00:00:03.550 --> 00:00:04.630
Kamui...

00:00:05.050 --> 00:00:07.450
Brother, I'm sorry, but I...

00:00:08.250 --> 00:00:12.090
I can't fight alongside him anymore.

00:00:12.410 --> 00:00:13.350
So I...

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:15.140
I'm sorry!

00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:16.450
Kamui!

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:21.080
Did you know that the national tournament 
is held on two days, today and next week?

00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:22.290
Y-Yes?

00:00:22.290 --> 00:00:24.290
The elimination rounds take place today,

00:00:24.530 --> 00:00:26.220
the first day.

00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:32.100
Right now, instead of chasing after him, 
maybe you should get through the preliminaries...

00:00:32.440 --> 00:00:34.920
and secure a place for him to come back to.

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:37.050
Kamui...

00:00:39.030 --> 00:00:41.140
Wait for us, Kamui...

00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:46.750
We'll make it through the preliminary 
rounds, then come and get you.

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:52.330
To bring you back to Team Quadrifoglio...

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:28.120
And now...

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:28.960
Vangua...

00:02:29.230 --> 00:02:32.700
We'll explain...

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:34.380
The progression of...

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:36.670
The Vanguard National Championship!

00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:43.730
Here we are at last, right?

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:44.440
Yes.

00:02:48.270 --> 00:02:50.620
Kourin!

00:02:50.620 --> 00:02:52.090
Us too?

00:02:52.090 --> 00:02:55.230
All right, everyone, together with me!

00:02:56.120 --> 00:02:58.690
Kourin!

00:02:57.630 --> 00:02:58.490
Morikawa!

00:02:58.690 --> 00:03:03.700
Jurassic Army

00:03:04.210 --> 00:03:09.130
As you all know, the elimination rounds 
will be held today, the opening day.

00:03:09.130 --> 00:03:11.040
And so, to start...

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:15.470
all 32 participating teams 
will be divided into 8 blocks.

00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:20.460
There are four teams in each block.

00:03:18.150 --> 00:03:20.460
Team A
Team B
Team C
Team D

00:03:20.460 --> 00:03:23.360
These four teams will 
fight round-robin style...

00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:26.720
and the top two teams will 
go on to play in the finals.

00:03:26.930 --> 00:03:30.360
How will those top two teams be decided?

00:03:30.360 --> 00:03:32.690
Well, in this example, in this 
outcome of the matches...

00:03:35.970 --> 00:03:40.340
Among the four teams in Block 1, 
Team A has 3 wins and 0 losses,

00:03:40.340 --> 00:03:42.390
while Team B has 2 wins and 1 loss.

00:03:42.690 --> 00:03:46.370
These two teams with superior 
performance advance to the finals.

00:03:46.370 --> 00:03:50.230
But what if results turn out the same?

00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:55.070
Then the win-loss records will be scrutinized 
more closely and a judgment call will be made.

00:03:55.070 --> 00:03:58.250
So that's how it'll be decided!

00:03:58.250 --> 00:04:01.540
Anyway, the strong teams will be chosen.

00:04:01.540 --> 00:04:05.900
But I'd like you to aim to be the strongest 
team on the block by winning all three matches!

00:04:06.350 --> 00:04:09.230
Do that and you'll definitely 
proceed to the finals!

00:04:09.230 --> 00:04:10.070
Right!

00:04:10.070 --> 00:04:12.920
Everyone, please do your best, okay?

00:04:12.920 --> 00:04:15.110
Yeah!!

00:04:15.110 --> 00:04:17.560
If we win all three matches, we'll qualify...

00:04:17.870 --> 00:04:20.180
We can move on to the next round immediately.

00:04:20.550 --> 00:04:23.860
Then we will advance to the following 
round, for Kamui's sake, too!

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:26.540
Please let me go first.

00:04:28.990 --> 00:04:32.080
I want to win this elimination 
round, no matter what it takes!

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:33.160
I will win!

00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:35.460
Aichi...

00:04:36.130 --> 00:04:38.550
In that case, I'll go second.

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:43.020
After all, I caused trouble for you guys 
at the regional tournament.

00:04:43.480 --> 00:04:44.930
Misaki...

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:49.360
Continuing on, I'll announce 
the block divisions.

00:04:49.360 --> 00:04:53.090
The groupings, as chosen randomly 
by our computer, are...

00:04:53.090 --> 00:04:54.320
This!

00:04:54.310 --> 00:04:56.560
Team Q4
Team Jurassic Army
Team Muscle Brain
Team FFAL4

00:04:54.810 --> 00:04:56.310
First, A Block!

00:04:56.560 --> 00:05:01.220
Oh! Q4 is the first team 
listed. That's a good omen!

00:05:01.220 --> 00:05:02.150
Look.

00:05:05.860 --> 00:05:09.830
Team FFAL4...?

00:05:09.830 --> 00:05:13.340
Team Foo Fighter AL4...

00:05:13.340 --> 00:05:16.310
They're last year's champions!

00:05:16.310 --> 00:05:19.870
Certainly, we met the leader 
of that team at PSY, didn't we?

00:05:27.630 --> 00:05:30.340
Yes. Ren Suzugamori...

00:05:30.340 --> 00:05:32.490
He was extremely strong...

00:05:32.490 --> 00:05:33.920
I see...

00:05:34.230 --> 00:05:35.950
That figures.

00:05:35.950 --> 00:05:39.900
But why did last year's winning 
team have to be in our block...?

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:42.380
Team Q4
Team Jurassic Army
Team Muscle Brain
Team FFAL4

00:05:40.340 --> 00:05:42.380
This is worrisome...

00:05:59.070 --> 00:06:01.620
Team Q4 is in A Block...

00:06:01.620 --> 00:06:02.900
Crap...

00:06:02.900 --> 00:06:04.060
Kamui the Great!

00:06:04.060 --> 00:06:05.210
We've been looking for you!

00:06:09.530 --> 00:06:10.890
Y-You've got the wrong guy.

00:06:11.190 --> 00:06:13.690
What are you talking about, Kamui the Great?

00:06:13.690 --> 00:06:15.880
That's Kamui the Great's 
characteristic fashion.

00:06:15.880 --> 00:06:18.640
And you've got that hot-blooded aura...

00:06:18.640 --> 00:06:20.980
There's no way we'd mistake 
somebody else for you.

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:22.020
Hot-blooded...

00:06:22.930 --> 00:06:24.390
Shoot!

00:06:24.390 --> 00:06:26.400
HBB! HBF!

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:29.340
Hot-blooded boy! Hot-blooded dope!

00:06:29.340 --> 00:06:32.230
I meant "dope" as a compliment!

00:06:32.230 --> 00:06:33.920
HD, yo!

00:06:34.390 --> 00:06:37.700
But today you've got kind 
of a timid aura mixed in...

00:06:37.700 --> 00:06:40.300
W-What was that, you guys?!

00:06:40.300 --> 00:06:43.130
You really want to rejoin 
your team, don't you?

00:06:43.130 --> 00:06:46.710
Kamui the Great, you wanted to be in 
this tournament more than any of 'em!

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:52.760
N-Not really. I don't wanna be 
in this stupid national tournament...

00:06:52.960 --> 00:06:56.130
Don't be a CC, but a TCG!

00:06:56.130 --> 00:06:59.970
Don't be a cool customer, but a 
totally cheerful guy like always!

00:06:59.970 --> 00:07:04.040
I don't care what anyone 
says, I am not going back.

00:07:04.040 --> 00:07:05.730
Kamui the Great!

00:07:06.180 --> 00:07:10.590
Instead, support Brother for me!

00:07:10.590 --> 00:07:13.280
That's my final request!

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:15.020
Kamui the Great!

00:07:15.020 --> 00:07:17.430
"FR"?! That's a bad omen!

00:07:18.830 --> 00:07:21.460
Kamui the Great!

00:07:21.890 --> 00:07:27.460
Okay... all teams, please 
proceed to the qualifying hall!

00:07:27.460 --> 00:07:30.550
Oh, the A Block hall is right here.

00:07:30.550 --> 00:07:32.340
Lucky!

00:07:32.340 --> 00:07:34.470
It is a pain having to move, isn't it?

00:07:34.470 --> 00:07:41.160
And now, the start of the national 
championship tournament elimination round fights!

00:07:42.840 --> 00:07:45.840
All Cardfighters who have gathered 
here from around the nation...

00:07:45.840 --> 00:07:48.550
Please show us some heated battles, okay?

00:07:48.550 --> 00:07:50.360
We're counting on you!

00:07:50.820 --> 00:07:53.540
Vanguard Fight!

00:07:53.540 --> 00:07:55.510
Vanguard!

00:07:59.730 --> 00:08:02.750
Team Caesar is in another block...

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:09.040
That's strange...

00:08:10.190 --> 00:08:11.590
He isn't here...

00:08:11.590 --> 00:08:16.560
Ren Suzugamori from Team Foo Fighter AL4...

00:08:18.990 --> 00:08:21.040
Long time no see, eh, Kai?

00:08:25.980 --> 00:08:27.060
Tetsu...

00:08:27.290 --> 00:08:29.020
What's wrong, Tetsu?

00:08:29.020 --> 00:08:30.380
A friend of yours?

00:08:30.380 --> 00:08:32.030
He's an old acquaintance.

00:08:35.230 --> 00:08:37.580
I've seen his picture in a magazine before!

00:08:38.540 --> 00:08:41.820
Those three kids are AL4!

00:08:45.700 --> 00:08:48.120
I didn't expect to meet you here.

00:08:49.600 --> 00:08:51.550
Why isn't Ren here?

00:08:52.450 --> 00:08:56.980
You really think Ren would bother showing up to 
the preliminary round of the national tournament?

00:08:56.980 --> 00:08:58.620
Even you know better.

00:08:59.120 --> 00:09:02.640
Do I? I've forgotten everything 
that happened back then.

00:09:03.170 --> 00:09:06.670
So, Kai knew Ren...

00:09:07.540 --> 00:09:09.360
It's got nothing to do with you!

00:09:10.880 --> 00:09:11.860
Sorry...

00:09:12.410 --> 00:09:14.320
So he'll be in the finals.

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:18.070
You'll probably be able to meet 
him if you make it to the finals.

00:09:19.240 --> 00:09:23.350
Ren is playing on two other teams, too.

00:09:23.350 --> 00:09:26.330
So there's no way you guys are 
going to get to the final round.

00:09:26.750 --> 00:09:29.390
The final match will be Foo 
Fighter versus Foo Fighter.

00:09:29.390 --> 00:09:31.090
It may as well be written in stone.

00:09:31.290 --> 00:09:32.590
He's playing on...

00:09:32.590 --> 00:09:33.840
...Two other teams?

00:09:34.400 --> 00:09:37.290
They've got a teammate who's that strong...

00:09:37.290 --> 00:09:38.910
Foo Fighter...

00:09:38.910 --> 00:09:40.700
Ren Suzugamori...

00:09:40.700 --> 00:09:42.250
Who exactly is he?!

00:09:46.480 --> 00:09:49.930
At any rate, I'll be glad 
to have a rematch with you.

00:09:50.430 --> 00:09:51.770
See you on the field.

00:09:57.530 --> 00:09:58.520
Kai...

00:09:58.850 --> 00:09:59.970
You heard, didn't you?

00:10:00.400 --> 00:10:02.760
I don't remember 
what happened back then...

00:10:04.240 --> 00:10:05.370
Kai!

00:10:05.740 --> 00:10:06.940
Leave him.

00:10:07.250 --> 00:10:08.580
Misaki...

00:10:08.580 --> 00:10:11.410
Everyone has something they 
don't want to talk about.

00:10:12.810 --> 00:10:15.440
Attention, please!

00:10:16.280 --> 00:10:21.020
All right, let's start our first 
round of the national tournament!

00:10:24.680 --> 00:10:29.560
The pairings for each block 
of the first round are here!

00:10:24.680 --> 00:10:29.560
Team Q4 vs Team Jurassic Army
Team Vainglory vs Team Grand Chariot

00:10:29.560 --> 00:10:32.950
Team Q4 versus Jurassic Army!

00:10:33.600 --> 00:10:35.150
That's us.

00:10:35.150 --> 00:10:38.230
For now, AL4 is still a ways off.

00:10:38.230 --> 00:10:39.070
Yeah...

00:10:39.400 --> 00:10:40.440
Aichi.

00:10:40.440 --> 00:10:41.160
Yes?

00:10:41.940 --> 00:10:45.700
Sooner or later, the day will come when 
you understand both Ren and Kai...

00:10:46.010 --> 00:10:47.130
But right now...

00:10:47.660 --> 00:10:52.030
let's concentrate on the fight. We're 
going to advance past this first round!

00:10:53.580 --> 00:10:55.160
Aichi, you're up first!

00:10:56.900 --> 00:10:57.700
Right!

00:11:03.830 --> 00:11:05.750
It is nerve-wracking, isn't it?

00:11:10.860 --> 00:11:15.370
Team Q4 Aichi Sendou vs Team Jurassic Army Gunji

00:11:11.610 --> 00:11:13.420
Vanguard National Championship...

00:11:13.420 --> 00:11:15.360
A Block...

00:11:15.670 --> 00:11:18.400
The first match of the first 
fight of the first round!

00:11:21.030 --> 00:11:22.900
Aichi Sendou vs...

00:11:22.900 --> 00:11:24.610
Ryudou Gunji!

00:11:29.890 --> 00:11:31.020
Brother...

00:11:40.360 --> 00:11:42.600
I haven't seen your face before,

00:11:42.600 --> 00:11:45.230
so perhaps this is your first time 
playing at a national tournament?

00:11:45.230 --> 00:11:46.100
Yes.

00:11:46.100 --> 00:11:49.100
I see... I like your expression.

00:11:49.100 --> 00:11:51.150
You're totally motivated.

00:11:51.150 --> 00:11:52.880
Thank you.

00:11:52.880 --> 00:11:54.390
However, boy...

00:11:55.260 --> 00:11:58.980
Motivation alone won't get you to the 
next round of the national tournament!

00:12:00.240 --> 00:12:02.360
Both Cardfighters, to your console!

00:12:03.740 --> 00:12:07.160
Um... I was confused at the 
regional tournament too, but...

00:12:07.810 --> 00:12:09.740
I'm in the right spot, right?

00:12:15.640 --> 00:12:19.230
It looks like this isn't his first 
time at the national tournament.

00:12:19.740 --> 00:12:21.340
He's full of confidence...

00:12:25.490 --> 00:12:28.160
But I can't lose...

00:12:28.840 --> 00:12:31.100
There's a reason I have to win!

00:12:32.350 --> 00:12:33.580
Brother...

00:12:47.900 --> 00:12:50.160
All right, begin the match!

00:13:04.500 --> 00:13:06.790
Stand up, Vanguard!

00:13:20.870 --> 00:13:23.170
Stand up, Vanguard!

00:13:29.450 --> 00:13:30.790
It's starting!

00:13:46.190 --> 00:13:48.010
Awesome!

00:13:52.680 --> 00:13:53.720
Barcgal!

00:13:55.110 --> 00:13:56.480
Dragon Egg!

00:13:56.830 --> 00:13:59.990
The first match has begun!

00:13:59.990 --> 00:14:06.420
I'm MC Miya and with me is Dr. O, 
who will be providing commentary.

00:14:06.420 --> 00:14:08.590
If it's about Vanguard, leave it to me.

00:14:08.990 --> 00:14:11.800
I'm a man who's dedicated 
his life to Vanguard!

00:14:11.800 --> 00:14:13.630
Doctor O!

00:14:13.630 --> 00:14:14.930
It's a pleasure to be here.

00:14:14.930 --> 00:14:21.320
Here in A Block, we have Team Q4 versus 
Jurassic Army, the first match!

00:14:21.710 --> 00:14:24.530
This is the first time I've seen Team Q4.

00:14:24.530 --> 00:14:26.620
What kind of fight will they show me?

00:14:26.920 --> 00:14:28.970
I'm so excited! I can't wait!

00:14:29.560 --> 00:14:31.790
My turn! I draw!

00:14:31.790 --> 00:14:33.950
I ride Sonic Noa!

00:14:36.770 --> 00:14:38.810
I activate Dragon Egg's skill!

00:14:39.020 --> 00:14:41.170
I move you to the rear-guard!

00:14:41.170 --> 00:14:43.430
That marks the end of my engagement!

00:14:43.430 --> 00:14:44.360
I'm starting!

00:14:45.830 --> 00:14:47.270
I ride Wingal!

00:14:50.650 --> 00:14:51.990
Barcgal moves!

00:14:54.130 --> 00:14:56.460
I call the Little Sage, Marron!

00:14:59.800 --> 00:15:01.370
With a boost from Barcgal...

00:15:01.590 --> 00:15:04.080
Wingal attacks Sonic Noa!

00:15:07.710 --> 00:15:08.910
Trigger check!

00:15:11.240 --> 00:15:12.920
Damage check!

00:15:14.110 --> 00:15:15.510
I attack with Marron, too!

00:15:20.710 --> 00:15:24.740
Sendou has quickly dealt damage.

00:15:25.060 --> 00:15:26.720
Certainly, things are 
going smoothly for him...

00:15:26.720 --> 00:15:28.890
But this is the national tournament.

00:15:29.190 --> 00:15:31.370
He can't let down his guard yet!

00:15:31.370 --> 00:15:33.570
I guess you're... excited?

00:15:33.570 --> 00:15:35.030
It's my turn!

00:15:37.000 --> 00:15:39.680
I ride Ravenous Dragon, Megarex!

00:15:42.270 --> 00:15:44.830
I call Cannon Fire Dragon, Cannon Gear!

00:15:47.830 --> 00:15:50.490
I activate Cannon Gear's skill!

00:15:51.820 --> 00:15:55.760
When Cannon Gear is called, one of 
its allies has to leave the field!

00:15:57.270 --> 00:16:00.430
Dragon Egg, sacrifice yourself!

00:16:01.720 --> 00:16:03.720
You sacrificed an ally?!

00:16:04.250 --> 00:16:08.470
There's no way around it. That's the only 
way Cannon Gear can step up to the front line.

00:16:09.340 --> 00:16:11.530
With powerful soldiers...

00:16:11.530 --> 00:16:14.720
They are worth sacrificing 
the weaker soldiers for.

00:16:15.280 --> 00:16:18.550
However, I won't let Dragon 
Egg's sacrifice be in vain!

00:16:18.550 --> 00:16:20.090
I activate its skill!

00:16:20.090 --> 00:16:21.710
Counterblast!

00:16:21.710 --> 00:16:23.870
Dragon Egg returns to my hand!

00:16:25.870 --> 00:16:28.990
If I do this, it returns to the battlefield.

00:16:28.990 --> 00:16:31.410
As a new reservist...

00:16:31.410 --> 00:16:36.050
Thus, it is possible for my army to advance endlessly!

00:16:36.500 --> 00:16:40.600
This is the true value of my Tachikaze deck!

00:16:40.820 --> 00:16:42.160
Whoa...

00:16:42.160 --> 00:16:45.940
That's right. His deck is powered up 
with Demonic Lord Invasion.

00:16:45.940 --> 00:16:48.350
What do you sound so proud about?!

00:16:48.900 --> 00:16:51.500
Come to think of it, that's 
your main unit, isn't it?

00:16:51.500 --> 00:16:52.320
Oh, that's what it's about!

00:16:53.490 --> 00:16:54.770
Be careful...

00:16:55.100 --> 00:16:58.070
My opponents are powerful, violent units.

00:16:59.020 --> 00:17:03.210
I call Wing Dragon, Skyptero 
and Pack Dragon, Tinyrex!

00:17:08.190 --> 00:17:09.020
Here it comes!

00:17:09.340 --> 00:17:11.800
I attack Wingal with Cannon Gear!

00:17:15.950 --> 00:17:17.090
No guard.

00:17:22.230 --> 00:17:23.980
Damage trigger check!

00:17:25.990 --> 00:17:27.980
I attack with Megarex!

00:17:31.150 --> 00:17:32.270
No guard!

00:17:33.960 --> 00:17:35.320
Drive check!

00:17:39.460 --> 00:17:41.360
With a boost from Tinyrex...

00:17:41.360 --> 00:17:43.700
I attack with Skyptero!

00:17:45.250 --> 00:17:46.540
No guard!

00:17:46.760 --> 00:17:51.290
Hey! All his attacks are getting through... 
What the heck is Aichi doing?!

00:18:00.160 --> 00:18:02.400
That marks the end of my engagement.

00:18:03.300 --> 00:18:06.330
Pathetic! 3 damage at one go!

00:18:07.600 --> 00:18:10.320
He's declaring no guard.

00:18:10.320 --> 00:18:12.940
He must be up to something.

00:18:13.500 --> 00:18:17.290
Uh-oh, what could Sendou be thinking?

00:18:17.660 --> 00:18:20.490
Well, let's watch closely...

00:18:23.960 --> 00:18:27.050
I dared to accumulate damage 
by having no guard...

00:18:27.050 --> 00:18:28.210
just for this purpose!

00:18:29.330 --> 00:18:32.510
Stand up, my avatar! I ride...

00:18:33.690 --> 00:18:35.810
Blaster Blade!

00:18:37.820 --> 00:18:39.180
I activate his skill!

00:18:39.670 --> 00:18:41.120
Counterblast!

00:18:43.860 --> 00:18:46.180
Cannon Gear, retire from the field!

00:18:52.480 --> 00:18:57.880
I see, boy. Your "no guard" declarations 
before were for this skill, eh?

00:18:58.520 --> 00:19:02.220
I took damage and used 
it for a Counterblast...

00:19:02.610 --> 00:19:04.000
And it worked well.

00:19:04.390 --> 00:19:06.440
Marron, move to the rear!

00:19:09.230 --> 00:19:12.820
I call the Knight of Truth, Gordon 
and Knight of Rose, Morgana!

00:19:19.810 --> 00:19:22.000
Morgana's power is 6000...

00:19:22.000 --> 00:19:24.550
And no units that can boost...

00:19:24.550 --> 00:19:27.770
He doesn't have enough 
power to attack Megarex...

00:19:28.100 --> 00:19:31.320
Then at least reduce his 
attacking power a little!

00:19:32.210 --> 00:19:34.590
I attack Skyptero with Morgana!

00:19:39.000 --> 00:19:41.740
Skyptero, activate your skill!

00:19:42.410 --> 00:19:44.240
Counterblast!

00:19:44.760 --> 00:19:47.600
Then Skyptero returns to my hand.

00:19:47.940 --> 00:19:50.790
I don't let soldiers in my army 
get sacrificed for nothing!

00:19:51.610 --> 00:19:53.150
With a boost from Barcgal...

00:19:54.010 --> 00:19:56.990
Blaster Blade attacks Megarex!

00:20:00.370 --> 00:20:02.080
Drive trigger check!

00:20:08.050 --> 00:20:10.820
With a boost from Marron, Gordon attacks!

00:20:13.350 --> 00:20:16.200
I won't allow it! I defend with Dragon Egg!

00:20:24.170 --> 00:20:25.730
My turn is over.

00:20:25.730 --> 00:20:27.910
I gave him 1 damage, huh?

00:20:27.910 --> 00:20:30.330
But I made Cannon Gear leave the field!

00:20:30.710 --> 00:20:34.010
I guess, for Aichi, he did okay...

00:20:34.010 --> 00:20:36.640
No, he's doing really well!

00:20:36.640 --> 00:20:38.970
I think it's gonna start from here...

00:20:39.880 --> 00:20:43.470
The real fear of the national 
championship, shining through...

00:20:43.800 --> 00:20:47.750
Okay, the preliminary skirmish, with both 
players taking a wait-and-see approach,

00:20:47.750 --> 00:20:49.300
is over as they move into the middle stage.

00:20:49.300 --> 00:20:51.290
From here on in, the units that are sent out

00:20:51.290 --> 00:20:53.800
will most likely be directly entwined 
with the outcome of the fight!

00:20:53.800 --> 00:20:54.980
Mm-hm!

00:20:54.980 --> 00:20:57.970
What kind of fight will 
both players show us?!

00:20:57.970 --> 00:20:59.850
Exciting, isn't it?!

00:20:59.850 --> 00:21:01.490
Is that all you have to say?

00:21:01.490 --> 00:21:05.250
Yes! There's nothing better than 
having fun watching the game.

00:21:05.250 --> 00:21:07.270
Oh, that's right! That's absolutely right-o!

00:21:09.070 --> 00:21:11.350
What are you doing, Shin?

00:21:11.350 --> 00:21:13.520
Huh?! I don't really know...

00:21:13.520 --> 00:21:15.570
I'm the manager.

00:21:16.070 --> 00:21:20.380
And while we're at a tournament, I'd 
be happy if you called me "Coach".

00:21:20.380 --> 00:21:22.640
Understood... Shin.

00:21:22.640 --> 00:21:24.090
Look...!

00:21:27.300 --> 00:21:30.810
Boy, you've brought Cannongear down admirably.

00:21:31.920 --> 00:21:35.350
But it's still too early to feel at ease.

00:21:35.350 --> 00:21:39.410
Even with losing Cannon Gear, my 
army stands as firm as a rock!

00:21:40.900 --> 00:21:44.700
Let's go to war, my strongest soldier!

00:21:45.430 --> 00:21:49.830
Glorious mechanical dragon! 
Gallop across the Earth!

00:21:49.830 --> 00:21:51.170
I ride...

00:21:51.170 --> 00:21:54.450
Tyrant Deathrex!

00:21:56.450 --> 00:21:57.750
Deathrex!

00:22:00.870 --> 00:22:03.020
That's definitely a powerful unit...

00:22:03.700 --> 00:22:08.070
But no matter how strong his 
units are, I'm not gonna lose!

00:22:08.640 --> 00:22:10.270
For Kamui's sake...

00:22:10.710 --> 00:22:12.220
And for the sake of my other teammates...

00:22:13.100 --> 00:22:16.450
I'm going to win this fight, no matter what!

00:23:51.240 --> 00:23:55.460
Deathrex... I remember having trouble 
with that when I fought against Izaki.

00:23:55.460 --> 00:23:57.330
Aichi, don't let your guard down!

00:23:57.330 --> 00:24:00.620
He's got a Tachikaze deck that's been built 
up with Demonic Lord Invasion boosters!

00:24:00.620 --> 00:24:03.000
I wonder how many grade 3 units he has...

00:24:03.000 --> 00:24:04.000
Morikawa!

00:24:04.000 --> 00:24:06.980
Go, Aichi! We're with you!

00:24:06.980 --> 00:24:10.730
He sacrificed his own units to increase 
his power. Now that's intense!

00:24:10.730 --> 00:24:13.470
Next time: Mad Dash Forward! Tachikaze Deck!

00:24:13.470 --> 00:24:16.360
I'm not gonna lose! I... We...

00:24:16.360 --> 00:24:18.970
I'm gonna meet Kamui with 
an image of victory!
